# lindsey-ghost-v2 — SSH-into-ghost variant of lindsey-v2
#
# Design intent: the background hue is rotated to ~H58 (warm umber), which is
# the near-complement of lindsey's H228 teal. Peripheral vision reads hue and
# temperature long before it reads detail, so a warm field is an instant
# "not my laptop" signal even when you aren't looking directly at the window.
#
# The 16 accent colors are deliberately IDENTICAL in hue and lightness to
# lindsey-v2. Syntax highlighting therefore means the same thing on both
# machines — red is still error, green is still string — so nothing has to be
# relearned. Only the ambient surface changes. The previous version failed
# because it was merely *darker* (bg L=9), which reads as "dim", not "different".
#
# Cursor is cyan here (vs orange in lindsey-v2) as a second independent cue.

